{
  "title": "Postgres: learning dashboard",
  "uid": "postgres-learning",
  "tags": [
    "postgres",
    "learning"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "editable": true,
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "label": "Prometheus",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus"
      },
      {
        "name": "instance",
        "label": "Server",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(pg_up, instance)",
          "refId": "instance"
        },
        "includeAll": false
      },
      {
        "name": "datname",
        "label": "Database",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(pg_database_size_bytes{instance=~\"$instance\"}, datname)",
          "refId": "datname"
        },
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": 1,
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 6
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "\n**Read top to bottom.** *Availability* and *Throughput* tell you **if** the database is hurting. *Queries*, *Memory vs disk* and *Tables* tell you **why**. *Vacuum & locks* are the slow-burning problems that turn into the fast ones.\n\n- Postgres's own statistics are **cumulative since the last reset**: `xact_commit`, `blks_read`, `seq_scan`, `pg_stat_statements_*_total` only go up. Wrap them in `rate()`. Sizes, `n_dead_tup`, connection counts and lock counts are gauges: graph them raw.\n- Alloy scrapes the exporter every 60s, and the exporter runs its SQL at scrape time. Anything shorter than a minute (a 10s lock, a burst of connections) can fall between two scrapes. For those, the Postgres logs are the source.\n- `pg_stat_statements` only gives a `queryid`. Get the SQL with `SELECT query FROM pg_stat_statements WHERE queryid = <id>;` in a database that has the extension (`users` here)\n- Only the series these panels use are sent (see `prometheus.relabel \"db\"` in `alloy.alloy`). If you add a panel and it's empty, add its metric to the allowlist.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Availability & connections",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Up",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "`pg_up`: whether the exporter could connect and run its queries on the last scrape.\n\n0 means the database is down, or the `monitoring` role can't log in. *No data* means Alloy itself stopped sending.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "DOWN",
                  "color": "red"
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "UP",
                  "color": "green"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "min(pg_up{instance=~\"$instance\"})",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "gauge",
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Connections used",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Client backends \u00f7 `max_connections`. The limit is server-wide, so this ignores the database filter.\n\nWhen it reaches 100%, new connections get `FATAL: sorry, too many clients already` and the app fails while Postgres looks idle. The usual fix is a pooler (PgBouncer) or smaller app pools, not a higher limit: every connection is a process with its own memory.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.7
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.9
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(pg_stat_activity_count{instance=~\"$instance\"}) / max(pg_settings_max_connections{instance=~\"$instance\"})",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 4,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Connections by state",
      "description": "From `pg_stat_activity`. `active` is running a query. `idle` is a pooled connection waiting. **`idle in transaction`** opened a transaction and isn't doing anything with it: it holds its locks and its snapshot, so vacuum can't clean anything newer.\n\nLook for: `idle in transaction` that stays above zero. It's almost always an app bug (a missing commit, or a request doing HTTP calls inside a transaction).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "max_connections"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dash",
                  "dash": [
                    10,
                    10
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.fillOpacity",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (state) (pg_stat_activity_count{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\", state!~\"disabled|fastpath function call|idle in transaction \\\\(aborted\\\\)\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{state}}",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max(pg_settings_max_connections{instance=~\"$instance\"})",
          "legendFormat": "max_connections",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Oldest open transaction",
      "description": "Age of the oldest transaction in each state, from `xact_start`.\n\nA long transaction holds back the xmin horizon: vacuum can't remove any row version deleted after it started, in **any** table. Long `idle in transaction` sessions are how tables bloat while autovacuum runs normally.\n\nLook for: minutes on an OLTP database. Reports and migrations can legitimately take long; `idle in transaction` never should.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max by (state) (pg_stat_activity_max_tx_duration{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\", state=~\"active|idle in transaction\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{state}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Throughput & errors",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 15,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Transactions per second",
      "description": "`xact_commit` rate: Postgres's equivalent of requests per second. Every statement outside an explicit `BEGIN` is its own transaction, so this counts statements in autocommit mode.\n\nLook for: drops with steady app traffic (the DB is stalling) and spikes (retry storms).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (datname) (rate(pg_stat_database_xact_commit{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{datname}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 9,
      "title": "Rollback ratio",
      "description": "Rolled back \u00f7 all transactions. Rollbacks are errors (constraint violations, serialization failures, statement timeouts) or app-initiated `ROLLBACK`.\n\nLook for: a change in the baseline. Some ORMs roll back read-only transactions on purpose, so the absolute value depends on the client.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (datname) (rate(pg_stat_database_xact_rollback{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval])) / (sum by (datname) (rate(pg_stat_database_xact_commit{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval])) + sum by (datname) (rate(pg_stat_database_xact_rollback{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{datname}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 6,
        "y": 16,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 10,
      "title": "Rows per second by operation",
      "description": "What the transactions actually do. `fetched` counts rows read through indexes and seq scans.\n\nLook for: `fetched` growing much faster than TPS. The same requests are reading more rows each, usually a table that grew under a query with no good index.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "rowsps",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(pg_stat_database_tup_fetched{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "fetched",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(pg_stat_database_tup_inserted{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "inserted",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(pg_stat_database_tup_updated{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "updated",
          "refId": "C"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(pg_stat_database_tup_deleted{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "deleted",
          "refId": "D"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 16,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 11,
      "title": "Deadlocks",
      "description": "Postgres detected a lock cycle and killed one of the transactions (`ERROR: deadlock detected`). Should be 0.\n\nThe Postgres log has both statements. The fix is to take locks in a consistent order across code paths.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 80,
            "drawStyle": "bars"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (datname) (increase(pg_stat_database_deadlocks{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{datname}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 18,
        "y": 16,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 12,
      "title": "Queries (pg_stat_statements)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 13,
      "title": "Top 10 queries by total time",
      "description": "Seconds of execution per second, per query shape: **where the database spends its time**. 1.0 means the equivalent of one core running that query nonstop.\n\nThis is the first panel to optimise against. A 2ms query called 5,000 times/s costs more than a 3s report run once a minute.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "topk(10, sum by (queryid) (rate(pg_stat_statements_seconds_total{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{queryid}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 25,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 14,
      "title": "Top 10 queries by mean latency",
      "description": "Total time \u00f7 calls for each query shape: what one execution costs. It's a mean, so one slow outlier among fast calls is hidden. `pg_stat_statements` has no percentiles.\n\nLook for: a query whose mean climbs over days with flat traffic. Its table is growing and the plan isn't scaling.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "topk(10, sum by (queryid) (rate(pg_stat_statements_seconds_total{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval])) / sum by (queryid) (rate(pg_stat_statements_calls_total{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{queryid}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 25,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 15,
      "title": "Top 10 queries by calls",
      "description": "Executions per second per query shape.\n\nLook for: a cheap query with a very high rate. That's usually N+1 (one query per row of a previous result) and is fixed in the app, not in the database.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "topk(10, sum by (queryid) (rate(pg_stat_statements_calls_total{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{queryid}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 25,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": 16,
      "title": "Query leaderboard (selected time range)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Every query shape over the dashboard's time range, sorted by total time. Copy a `queryid` and run `SELECT query FROM pg_stat_statements WHERE queryid = <id>;` in a database that has the extension (`users` here) to get the SQL.\n\nHigh **rows / call** on a query that returns a few rows to the app means it's filtering or aggregating a lot of data in the database.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Total time"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "s"
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.cellOptions",
                "value": {
                  "type": "gauge",
                  "mode": "basic"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Calls"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "short"
              },
              {
                "id": "decimals",
                "value": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Mean"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "s"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Rows / call"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "decimals",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "sortBy": [
          {
            "displayName": "Total time",
            "desc": true
          }
        ],
        "cellHeight": "sm"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (queryid) (increase(pg_stat_statements_seconds_total{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "format": "table"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (queryid) (increase(pg_stat_statements_calls_total{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "B",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "format": "table"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (queryid) (increase(pg_stat_statements_rows_total{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "C",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "format": "table"
        }
      ],
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "merge",
          "options": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "calculateField",
          "options": {
            "mode": "binary",
            "binary": {
              "left": "Value #A",
              "operator": "/",
              "right": "Value #B"
            },
            "alias": "Mean"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "calculateField",
          "options": {
            "mode": "binary",
            "binary": {
              "left": "Value #C",
              "operator": "/",
              "right": "Value #B"
            },
            "alias": "Rows / call"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true,
              "Value #C": true
            },
            "renameByName": {
              "Value #A": "Total time",
              "Value #B": "Calls"
            },
            "indexByName": {
              "queryid": 0,
              "Value #A": 1,
              "Value #B": 2,
              "Mean": 3,
              "Rows / call": 4
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 33,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 17,
      "title": "Memory vs disk",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 42,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 18,
      "title": "Cache hit ratio",
      "description": "Share of block reads served from `shared_buffers` instead of the OS. A miss isn't necessarily a disk read, since the OS page cache sits underneath, but it's the best signal Postgres has.\n\nOLTP should sit at ~99%. A sustained drop means the working set has outgrown memory, or a new query is scanning something large.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (datname) (rate(pg_stat_database_blks_hit{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval])) / (sum by (datname) (rate(pg_stat_database_blks_hit{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval])) + sum by (datname) (rate(pg_stat_database_blks_read{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{datname}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 43,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 19,
      "title": "Temp files written",
      "description": "Sorts, hashes and materialisations that didn't fit in `work_mem` and spilled to disk.\n\nLook for: anything sustained. Find the query in the leaderboard and run `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)`: a `Sort Method: external merge` or a batched hash join is the spill. Raise `work_mem` for that query or session, not globally: it's per sort node, per connection.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Bps",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (datname) (rate(pg_stat_database_temp_bytes{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{datname}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 43,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 20,
      "title": "Reads outside shared_buffers by table",
      "description": "Blocks read for the table's heap and indexes that weren't in `shared_buffers`, \u00d78 KiB per block. It shows **which** table is behind a drop in the cache hit ratio.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Bps",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "topk(10, 8192 * sum by (relname) (rate(pg_statio_user_tables_heap_blocks_read{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval]) + rate(pg_statio_user_tables_idx_blocks_read{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{relname}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 43,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 21,
      "title": "Tables & indexes",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 51,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 22,
      "title": "Rows read by sequential scans",
      "description": "Rows read by full table scans, per table. A seq scan on a small table is normal (cheaper than an index). Millions of rows/s on a big one is a missing index.\n\nLook for: a large table near the top. Find the query in the leaderboard and check its `WHERE` columns.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "rowsps",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "topk(10, sum by (relname) (rate(pg_stat_user_tables_seq_tup_read{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{relname}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 52,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 23,
      "title": "Index scan share",
      "description": "Index scans \u00f7 all scans per table. It counts scans, not rows, so read it next to the panel on the left: 99% index scans can still lose to the 1% of seq scans if each reads the whole table.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (relname) (rate(pg_stat_user_tables_idx_scan{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval])) / (sum by (relname) (rate(pg_stat_user_tables_idx_scan{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval])) + sum by (relname) (rate(pg_stat_user_tables_seq_scan{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{relname}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 6,
        "y": 52,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 24,
      "title": "Largest tables (table + indexes)",
      "description": "Size on disk, including dead tuples. Growth with steady row counts (see the dead tuples panel) is bloat, not data.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "topk(10, sum by (relname) (pg_stat_user_tables_table_size_bytes{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"} + pg_stat_user_tables_index_size_bytes{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"}))",
          "legendFormat": "{{relname}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 52,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 25,
      "title": "Database size",
      "description": "Everything in the database. On a managed server, compare it with the provisioned storage: running out of disk stops writes, and growing storage is usually one-way.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (datname) (pg_database_size_bytes{instance=~\"$instance\", datname=~\"$datname\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{datname}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 18,
        "y": 52,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 8
      }
